T*
(Tashkent House Price Predictor) Tj
T*
(Real Estate | Technical Project Brief) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Track: Field-Based Scenario) Tj
T*
(Client: Real estate stakeholders in Tashkent (buyers, sellers, agents, analysts)) Tj
T*
(Purpose: Design and implement a supervised machine learning solution that predicts residential property prices in Tashkent to improve price transparency and support data-driven decisions in the local [...]) Tj
T*
(---) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Client Background) Tj
T*
(--------------------) Tj
T*
(Tashkent is undergoing rapid urbanization, producing a dynamic and often opaque real estate market. Buyers, sellers, and local agents often rely on anecdotal knowledge and agent estimates when valuing[...]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Business Problem) Tj
T*
(-------------------) Tj
T*
(There is no standardized, data-driven method to estimate fair market prices for residential properties in Tashkent. This information asymmetry leads to:) Tj
T*
(- Buyers possibly overpaying due to lack of comparable objective estimates.) Tj
T*
(- Sellers underpricing or being unable to justify their asking price.) Tj
T*
(- Agents and analysts relying on intuition rather than reproducible analysis.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The business need is a transparent, reproducible pricing tool that estimates property values from observable characteristics to reduce information asymmetry and increase market confidence.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Requested Solution) Tj
T*
(---------------------) Tj
T*
(Develop a supervised regression solution to predict residential property prices in Tashkent using the publicly available "House Prices in Tashkent" dataset (Kaggle, Apache 2.0). Deliverables should in[...]) Tj
T*
(- A reproducible end-to-end Colab notebook demonstrating data processing, model training, evaluation, and inference.) Tj
T*
(- A saved model and preprocessing pipeline for inference (model.pkl).) Tj
T*
(- Documentation (dataset license/notes, evaluation results, limitations).) Tj
T*
(- A demo inference helper (e.g., predict() function) for quick price estimates on new properties.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Available Information) Tj
T*
(------------------------) Tj
T*
(Dataset: "House Prices in Tashkent" (Kaggle) — Apache 2.0 license.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Key fields available and used:) Tj
T*
(- Location: District or neighborhood (categorical)) Tj
T*
(- Total_Area_sqm: Total area in square meters (numeric)) Tj
T*
(- Rooms: Number of rooms (numeric)) Tj
T*
(- Floor: Floor number of the unit (numeric)) Tj
T*
(- Total_Flats (Total number of floors in the building) (numeric)) Tj
T*
(- Price: Target variable (numeric, UZS)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Notes:) Tj
T*
(- Data is publicly available and contains anonymized property listings.) Tj
T*
(- No personally identifiable information (PII) is present.) Tj
T*
(- Additional metadata (if present) must be reviewed for leakage risk.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Data & Problem Discovery — Complete Before Modeling) Tj
T*
(------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(Decision / Question | Student Response) Tj
T*
(:--- | :---) Tj
T*
(Selected dataset and source | Dataset: "House Prices in Tashkent" (Kaggle). Source: Kaggle dataset page. License: Apache 2.0.) Tj
T*
(What does one record / sample represent? | One record = single residential property listing in Tashkent with features and listed/recorded price.) Tj
T*
(Proposed target or ML objective | Supervised regression. Target: Price (UZS). Objective: Predict numeric price from property features.) Tj
T*
(Key information available at prediction / inference time | Location (district), Total_Area_sqm, Rooms, Floor, Total_Flats — all available at inference and do not rely on the target.) Tj
T*
(Main data quality issues | Check for: missing values, inconsistent district names/spellings, outliers (area, price), invalid floor values, and imbalanced district representation. Numeric features may [...]) Tj
T*
(Potential leakage risks | Avoid features derived from the target (e.g., price per sqm). If any target-derived encodings or post-sale metadata exist, exclude them to prevent leakage.) Tj
T*
(Privacy / fairness / licensing concerns | Dataset is under Apache 2.0 and anonymized. Evaluate fairness by inspecting per-district error distributions — ensure model does not systematically under/ov[...]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6. Technical Proposal — Complete Before Full Implementation) Tj
T*
(-----------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(Decision / Question | Student Response) Tj
T*
(:--- | :---) Tj
T*
(ML problem formulation | Supervised regression: learn mapping f(features) → Price.) Tj
T*
(Proposed baseline | Linear Regression (Ordinary Least Squares). Use Ridge variant as a robust baseline if regularization helps.) Tj
T*
(Main modeling approach(es) to investigate | Linear Regression (baseline), Random Forest Regressor (tree ensemble), XGBoost Regressor (gradient boosting). Compare models and consider ensembling if bene[...] ) Tj
T*
(Data splitting / validation strategy | Hold-out: 80% train / 20% test. On training set use k-fold cross-validation (e.g., 5-fold) for hyperparameter tuning. Consider grouped or stratified splitting by[...]) Tj
T*
(Primary evaluation metric(s) and why | Primary: Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE) — interpretable in UZS. Secondary: R-squared (R²) and Mean Absolute Error (MAE) for outlier-robustness. Report per-dis[...]) Tj
T*
(Expected inference input | JSON or dict with: { Location, Total_Area_sqm, Rooms, Floor, Total_Flats }. Input is preprocessed with same pipeline used in training.) Tj
T*
(Expected inference output | Single numeric predicted Price (UZS). Additionally, return a confidence estimate (e.g., prediction interval or a flag if input is out-of-distribution.) ) Tj
T*
(Main technical risks / assumptions | Dataset representativeness for current market; limited features (no year built, condition) constrain granularity; sparse data in some districts may limit accuracy.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(7. Functional Requirements) Tj
T*
(--------------------------) Tj
T*
(Requirement | How the project satisfies it) Tj
T*
(:--- | :---) Tj
T*
(Provide a quantitative price estimate for a property | Regression model returns numeric price prediction in UZS for given features.) Tj
T*
(Reproducibility and explainability | Provide Colab notebook, pinned requirements.txt, saved preprocessing+model pipeline. Use feature importance and SHAP to explain model behavior.) Tj
T*
(Easy to use and test | Provide demo.ipynb with a predict() helper function and example inputs; include sample scripts showing how to load model.pkl and run predictions.) Tj
T*
(Useful for client context | Estimates are in local currency with RMSE context and per-district reliability notes to help buyers, sellers, and agents use results appropriately.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(8. Expected Deliverables) Tj
T*
(------------------------) Tj
T*
(Deliverable | How it will be delivered) Tj
T*
(:--- | :---) Tj
T*
(Working ML solution | demo.ipynb (Google Colab) implementing end-to-end pipeline and demo inference.) Tj
T*
(Trained model or ML pipeline | model.pkl (scikit-learn Pipeline or serialized artifact bundling preprocessing + model).) Tj
T*
(Dataset documentation | data/README.md with dataset source URL, license (Apache 2.0), field descriptions, and preprocessing decisions.) Tj
T*
(Evaluation results | Test-set RMSE, MAE, R² for Linear Regression, Random Forest, and XGBoost; cross-validation summaries and per-district error analysis.) Tj
T*
(Inference interface | predict() function in demo.ipynb; optional small Gradio demo if requested.) Tj
T*
(Reproducible repository | Full GitHub repo with notebooks, requirements.txt, README, saved model, and submission/PROJECT_BRIEF.md.) Tj
T*
(Limitations & recommendations | Documented section outlining limits (geography, features), fairness checks, and suggestions for future data collection and model improvements.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(9. Acceptance Criteria) Tj
T*
(----------------------) Tj
T*
(Acceptance Criterion | How the project satisfies it) Tj
T*
(:--- | :---) Tj
T*
(Processes previously unseen input | Saved preprocessing pipeline + model can accept new property features and return a price prediction.) Tj
T*
(Output is meaningful for the client | Predictions are presented in UZS with RMSE context and per-district reliability notes.) Tj
T*
(Methodology and evaluation are explainable | Notebook documents preprocessing, modeling, tuning, and evaluation; includes feature importance and SHAP visualizations.) Tj
T*
(Reproducible | Colab notebook, pinned dependencies, and fixed random seeds are provided to reproduce experiments.) Tj
T*
(Known limitations, risks, and assumptions documented | Brief and data/README.md include limitations, representativeness concerns, and potential biases.) Tj
T*
(Implementation runs per documentation | README contains step-by-step instructions to reproduce training and inference locally or in Colab.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(10. Constraints) Tj
T*
(---------------) Tj
T*
(In Scope (What this project includes)) Tj
T*
(- Build and evaluate regression models (Linear Regression, Random Forest, XGBoost) on the Kaggle "House Prices in Tashkent" dataset.) Tj
T*
(- Provide a reproducible Colab notebook and serialized model/pipeline for inference.) Tj
T*
(- Perform basic fairness and per-district error analysis to identify significant bias or blind spots.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Out of Scope (What this project does NOT include)) Tj
T*
(- Full production deployment (no hosted web or mobile application).) Tj
T*
(- Real-time integration with live listing APIs.) Tj
T*
(- Detailed appraisal-level features (e.g., interior condition, exact address-level micro-pricing) unless additional data is provided.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(11. Questions You Must Resolve) Tj
T*
(------------------------------) Tj
T*
(1. Which features are most important for predicting house prices?  ) Tj
T*
(- Answer approach: compute feature importance (Random Forest / XGBoost) and SHAP values; surface top 5 drivers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. How well does the model generalize across different districts in Tashkent?  ) Tj
T*
(- Answer approach: per-district RMSE/MAE and bias analysis; produce maps or tables showing district-level errors.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. How many and which features are sufficient?  ) Tj
T*
(- Answer approach: incremental feature selection and model comparisons; consider recursive feature elimination or L1-regularized baselines.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. What is an acceptable prediction error for practical use?  ) Tj
T*
(- Answer approach: contextualize RMSE relative to median/mean price and stakeholder expectations; propose thresholds for “useful” vs “warning” predictions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. How can predictions be explained to a non-technical user?  ) Tj
T*
(- Answer approach: present the top 3 contributing features for a specific prediction, show expected error range, and include clear textual guidance in the demo.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6. How to detect and handle out-of-distribution inputs?  ) Tj
T*
(- Answer approach: implement input validation and range checks; warn when inputs fall outside training ranges and avoid overconfident intervals.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(---) Tj
T*
(Appendix — Quick Implementation Notes) Tj
T*
(-------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(- Preprocessing pipeline:) Tj
T*
(  - Clean and normalize district names, handle missing values, validate floor ≤ total_floors.) Tj
T*
(  - Numeric scaling for Linear Regression (StandardScaler); tree models not required to scale.) Tj
T*
(  - Encode Location: One-Hot Encoding for interpretable baselines; consider target (mean) encoding with nested CV to avoid leakage for tree-based models if district cardinality is high.) Tj
T*
(  - Use sklearn Pipeline to bundle preprocessing + model for safe serialization.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Baselines & models:) Tj
T*
(  - Baseline: Linear Regression (OLS) and Ridge variant for stability.) Tj
T*
(  - Tree-based: RandomForestRegressor (sklearn) and XGBoost XGBRegressor.) Tj
T*
(  - Hyperparameter search: RandomizedSearchCV or GridSearchCV with 5-fold CV on training set.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Explainability:) Tj
T*
(  - Feature importance (tree impurity and permutation importance).) Tj
T*
(  - SHAP values for local explanations (XGBoost/RandomForest).) Tj
